items.body:
The test setup relies on hard-coded coordinates and implicit default sizes (Task 100x80, BoundaryEvent 36x36) plus the internal `ATTACH_ORIENTATION_PADDING` behavior to guarantee a corner attachment. This makes the test brittle if default sizing or padding logic changes. Consider deriving positions from the created shapes’ actual bounds (width/height/mid) so the corner/axis-aligned conditions are ensured without depending on those internal constants.
```suggestion
          // create a task at an arbitrary position
          var task = elementFactory.createShape({
            type: 'bpmn:Task',
            x: 100,
            y: 100
          });
          canvas.addShape(task, rootElement);

          // place a boundary event so that its mid lies beyond the task's
          // right and bottom edges, guaranteeing a true bottom-right corner
          // orientation regardless of default sizes or padding constants
          var boundaryEvent = elementFactory.createShape({
            type: 'bpmn:BoundaryEvent'
          });

          var beWidth = boundaryEvent.width,
              beHeight = boundaryEvent.height;

          var beMidX = task.x + task.width + 1,
              beMidY = task.y + task.height + 1;

          boundaryEvent.x = beMidX - beWidth / 2;
          boundaryEvent.y = beMidY - beHeight / 2;
          boundaryEvent.host = task;

          canvas.addShape(boundaryEvent, rootElement);

          // place the target task so that its center x matches the boundary
          // event center x (strict vertical alignment), and it is below the
          // boundary event
          var boundaryMid = getMid(boundaryEvent);

          var targetTask = elementFactory.createShape({
            type: 'bpmn:Task'
          });

          var ttWidth = targetTask.width,
              ttHeight = targetTask.height;

          var targetMidX = boundaryMid.x,
              targetMidY = boundaryMid.y + ttHeight * 2;

          targetTask.x = targetMidX - ttWidth / 2;
          targetTask.y = targetMidY - ttHeight / 2;
```

