This new test asserts only that the connection has 2 waypoints. That can still pass even if the line is not actually straight/axis-aligned. Consider also asserting that the two waypoints share the same x (vertical) or y (horizontal) coordinate (or otherwise assert the expected docking/waypoints) so the test verifies the intended layout, not just the absence of extra points.
```suggestion
          expect(connection.waypoints).to.have.length(2);

          var start = connection.waypoints[0],
              end = connection.waypoints[1];

          // ensure the line is strictly vertical (axis-aligned), not diagonal
          expect(start.x).to.equal(end.x);
```

